> 
> Adaptation evidence is globally uneven, with the US, China, India and Brazil generating vastly more estimates than most countries. Key gaps also affect the measurement of costs and benefits. Engineering estimates often consider building costs alone, omitting welfare effects, labour-reallocation costs, labour-market frictions and non-monetary social and cultural costs. Residual damages should also be incorporated: among the **22 quantitatively synthesised studies, only four** include residual economic damages after adaptation.
